          <!-- Preamble Highlight Box -->
          <div
            style="background: #faf5ff; border-left: 4px solid #70146e; padding: 20px 22px; border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; margin-bottom: 30px;">
            <p style="color: #334155; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">
              In compliance with the Reserve Bank of India (Non-Banking Financial Companies – Know Your Customer)
              Directions, 2025
              <strong>(RBI/DOR/2025-26/361; DOR.AML.REC.No.280/14.01.003/2025-26 dated November 28, 2025)</strong> as
              <em>amended from time to time, the Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 (“PMLA”)</em> and the
              Prevention of Money-Laundering (Maintenance of Records) Rules, 2005, the Board of Directors of
              <strong>Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 (PMLA)</strong>, the Board of Directors of
              <strong>Lord Krishna Financial Services Ltd (“Company”)</strong> operating under the trade name
              <strong>“Prest Loans”</strong>
              has adopted this comprehensive KYC &amp; AML Policy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-doc">

            <!-- 1. Objective -->
            <div style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;">
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #70146e; margin-bottom: 10px;">1. Objectives of the
                Policy</h3>
              <p>The primary objectives of our KYC &amp; AML policy framework are:</p>
              <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.7; color: #475569;">
                <li>To prevent the Company from being used, intentionally or unintentionally, by criminal elements for
                  money laundering or terrorist financing activities.</li>
                <li>To establish robust Customer Identification Procedures (CIP) for establishing the identity of
                  borrowers before granting credit facilities.</li>
                <li>To put in place an effective risk categorization and transaction monitoring mechanism commensurate
                  with the borrower's profile.</li>
                <li>To ensure compliance with all statutory reporting requirements to the Financial Intelligence Unit -
                  India (FIU-IND) and the RBI.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- 2. Four Key Elements of KYC -->
            <div style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;">
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #70146e; margin-bottom: 14px;">2. The Four Pillars
                of KYC &amp; AML Governance</h3>

              <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 14px;">
                <div style="background: #fdf2f8; border: 1px solid #fbcfe8; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px;">
                  <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; color: #9d174d; margin: 0 0 6px;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-user-check"></i> Pillar 1: Customer Acceptance Policy (CAP)
                  </h4>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
                    Clear criteria for accepting customers. No loan account opened in anonymous, fictitious, or 'benami'
                    names.
                    Checks against UN, MHA, and international sanctions lists.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px;">
                  <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; color: #1d4ed8; margin: 0 0 6px;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-address-card"></i> Pillar 2: Customer Identification Procedure (CIP)
                  </h4>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
                    Rigorous verification of borrower identity and address using Officially Valid Documents (OVDs),
                    digital e-KYC, video verification, and legal business existence proofs.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px;">
                  <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; color: #15803d; margin: 0 0 6px;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high"></i> Pillar 3: Risk Management Framework
                  </h4>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
                    Grading customers into Low, Medium, and High-risk categories based on turnover, geography, business
                    activity,
                    and Politically Exposed Person (PEP) status.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #fff7ed; border: 1px solid #fed7aa; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px;">
                  <h4 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; color: #c2410c; margin: 0 0 6px;">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-chart"></i> Pillar 4: Transaction Monitoring
                  </h4>
                  <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
                    Continuous supervision of repayments, high-value early prepayments, cash velocity, and filing of
                    Suspicious Transaction Reports (STRs) with FIU-IND.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 3. Customer Identification Documents (OVDs Table) -->
            <div style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;">
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #70146e; margin-bottom: 12px;">3. Officially Valid
                Documents (OVD) Matrix</h3>
              <p>Borrowers must furnish verified copies of documents based on their constitution:</p>

              <div class="soc-table-card" style="margin-top: 16px;">
                <div class="soc-table-wrapper">
                  <table class="amortization-table" style="width: 100%;">
                    <thead>
                      <tr>
                        <th style="width: 25%;">Borrower Category</th>
                        <th style="width: 35%;">Proof of Identity (POI)</th>
                        <th style="width: 40%;">Proof of Address (POA) &amp; Business Proof</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                      <tr>
                        <td><strong>Individuals / Proprietors</strong></td>
                        <td>Aadhaar Card (masked), Passport, Voter ID Card, Driving License, PAN Card</td>
                        <td>Electricity Bill, Telephone/Broadband Bill, Bank Statement (last 3-6 months), Property tax
                          receipt</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td><strong>Sole Proprietorships</strong></td>
                        <td>PAN of Proprietor, Identity Proof of Proprietor</td>
                        <td>Registration certificate, GST Certificate, Municipal Trade License, Shop &amp; Establishment
                          Certificate, Udyam Registration</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td><strong>Partnership Firms &amp; LLPs</strong></td>
                        <td>PAN Card of Firm/LLP, Identity Proof of all Partners/Designated Partners</td>
                        <td>Partnership Deed, LLP Agreement, Registration Certificate with Registrar of Firms, Power of
                          Attorney in favor of signing partner</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td><strong>Private &amp; Public Companies</strong></td>
                        <td>PAN Card of Company, Identity Proof of Managing Director &amp; Authorized Signatories</td>
                        <td>Certificate of Incorporation (CIN), Memorandum &amp; Articles of Association (MOA &amp;
                          AOA), Board Resolution authorizing loan, List of Directors</td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td><strong>Trusts &amp; Societies</strong></td>
                        <td>PAN Card of Trust/Society, Identity Proof of Trustees/Founders</td>
                        <td>Trust Deed, Registration Certificate, Resolution of Managing Committee to avail loan</td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 4. Beneficial Ownership (BO) -->
            <div style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;">
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #70146e; margin-bottom: 10px;">4. Beneficial
                Ownership (BO) Identification</h3>
              <p>
                In compliance with PMLA Rules, the Company identifies the natural person(s) who ultimately own or
                control the legal entity borrowing funds:
              </p>
              <ul style="padding-left: 20px; line-height: 1.7; color: #475569;">
                <li><strong>For Companies:</strong> Any individual holding an ultimate controlling ownership interest of
                  more than <strong>10%</strong> of shares or voting rights.</li>
                <li><strong>For Partnership Firms &amp; LLPs:</strong> Any natural person owning or entitled to more
                  than <strong>15%</strong> of capital or profits.</li>
                <li><strong>For Unincorporated Associations / Trusts:</strong> Any natural person owning more than
                  <strong>15%</strong> of property or acting as Author, Settlor, or Trustee.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- 5. Principal Officer & FIU-IND Reporting -->
            <div style="margin-bottom: 28px; padding-bottom: 10px;">
              <h3 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: #70146e; margin-bottom: 10px;">5. Appointment of
                Principal Officer &amp; AML Reporting</h3>
              <p>
                The Company has appointed a designated Senior Executive as the <strong>Principal Officer</strong>
                responsible for overseeing
                AML policy implementation, staff training, and reporting obligations to the <strong>Financial
                  Intelligence Unit - India (FIU-IND)</strong>:
              </p>
              <div
                style="background: #faf5ff; border: 1px solid rgba(112, 20, 110, 0.2); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-top: 14px;">
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #334155;">
                  <strong>Principal Officer (AML &amp; KYC Compliance):</strong><br>
                  Lord Krishna Financial Services Limited ("Prest Loans")<br>
                  M5-M6, Essel House, 10 Asaf Ali Road, New Delhi - 110002<br>
                  Suspicious Transaction Reports (STRs) and Cash Transaction Reports (CTRs) are furnished directly to
                  Director, FIU-IND under PMLA.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

